WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.148
The Team Board is a shared board for planning and running one team’s work. In this video, you’ll plan from the backlog, set up a sprint, and move work across the board.

00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:19.937
Open Team Board, and pick a team. The Backlog tab lists everything that’s waiting for this team, with its type, due date, status, and who’s on it.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:29.915
If you work in sprints, the current one sits at the top, with its goal and dates. Move tickets into it, a few at a time or in bulk, and New sprint plans the next one.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:35.807
Columns lets you choose what the list shows, like priority, components, or the target release.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:44.779
Kanban Board shows the same tickets as cards, in a column for each stage. Drag a card to the next column as the work moves on.

00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:54.919
Each ticket type keeps its own stages, so a checklist and a maintenance request move the way they should. Filter by person, type, or priority to focus.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:01:05.159
Every card opens the full ticket, so the board is where the team runs its week. Each team has its own board, so the kitchen and the front of house can work their own way.

